01:26:17,348 --> 01:26:29,042
If absolutely everything goes smoothly, which, honestly, it genuinely does the overwhelming majority of

463
01:26:29,342 --> 01:26:41,036
the time in practice, a brand new certificate is fully issued and safely in

464
01:26:41,336 --> 01:26:48,018
place well before day ninety ever actually arrives.

465
01:26:48,318 --> 01:27:00,012
If something does go wrong at that first attempt, a DNS validation hiccup, a

466
01:27:00,312 --> 01:27:12,006
brief, temporary rate limit from the issuer, you still, genuinely have nearly a full

467
01:27:12,306 --> 01:27:24,001
month of real, comfortable runway remaining to notice, diagnose, and properly fix the underlying

468
01:27:24,301 --> 01:27:35,159
issue, calmly, well before anything in production actually, genuinely breaks for real users.

469
01:27:35,459 --> 01:27:47,153
Here's a genuinely useful discipline worth adopting directly, specifically around your Prometheus alert thresholds

470
01:27:47,453 --> 01:27:48,353
here.

